WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.780
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.780
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.780
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:44.310
Chapter 11

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:44.310
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:52.290
On December 1st of Space Year 794,
Imperial Year 485...

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:58.070
...the Free Planets Alliance finally deployed its
main fleet at the front gate of Iserlohn Fortress.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.760
The enemy fleet is currently
out of the Thor Hammer's range.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.750
They've halted 6.4
light seconds away.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.610
The number of ships
is approximately 30,000.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.950
Deploy our fleet.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.900
Drag the enemy into the
Thor Hammer's range.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.090
The size of the Imperial Fleet
was approximately 20,000 ships.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.380
Judging from the numbers, the
Alliance seems to have the advantage...

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.650
...but the Empire had Iserlohn
Fortress on their side.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.900
Especially since its main
cannon, the Thor Hammer...

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.100
...can destroy entire
fleets with one shot.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:45.190
In the past, the Alliance has been defeated
many times because of that cannon.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:51.690
What the Alliance had learned
from their bitter losses...

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:57.300
...was to measure the precise range of the cannon and to maneuver their fleet just outside that range...

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.990
...in order to lure the enemy fleet
into coming out of their formation.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:07.300
In the 5th Battle of Iserlohn two years ago,
the commander, Admiral Sidney Sitolet...

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:12.900
...using 50,000 ships for his operation, lured
the Imperial Fleet out of the cannon's range...

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.850
...and closed in on the fortress through
parallel pursuit of those enemy ships.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:23.050
But in the end, the Empire eradicated
the Alliance Fleet by using the cannon...

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.820
...sacrificing its own
fleet in the process.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:32.100
But nonetheless, the battle proved that the
Alliance held advantage over the Empire...

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.140
...in terms of its ability
to maneuver its fleet.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.970
Open fire !

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.000
On the other hand, the basic
strategy of the Imperial Fleet...

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.800
...is to lure the opposition
inside the main cannon's range.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.950
Moreover, since they don't want to be
destroyed by the Thor Hammer themselves...

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:54.450
...their ships will deploy on the corners, leaving the center empty, launching attacks in such a way...

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.450
...as to force the enemy ships to
concentrate in that center section.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.900
In such a formation, ships enter the combat, competing over the best positioning...

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.110
...in accordance with respective strategies.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:10.440
At this time Reinhard's fleet was in the rear as reserve and had not entered the fray.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.340
Because of that, it was easier
to see the whole battlefield...

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.270
...and Reinhard was able to precisely
decode the strategy of the Alliance Fleet.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.100
That's not a
bad plan at all.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.370
But the enemy has
made one miscalculation.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.760
Which is ?

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.740
That I'm here at Iserlohn.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.590
My fleet has only
about 2,200 ships.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:37.650
This is insignificant strategically, but
tactically speaking, it's quite important.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.230
That wasn't a slip
of the tongue, Kircheis.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:48.410
Speaking at the strategic
level, it's only 2,200 ships...

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:51.770
...but this fleet of 2,200
ships will save Iserlohn.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:59.540
There has never been a time when
Lord Reinhard spoke without basis.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.060
Petition Fleet Headquarters
for permission to launch.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.410
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:09.390
It's almost time, isn't it ?

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:09.990
Yes.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.110
Incoming missiles !

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.450
They'll be direct hits !

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.270
What ?

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.770
Why did you
allow direct hits ?

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.150
They used the dead angle.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.990
The movement of their
main fleet was a diversion !

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.470
The inner wall
is now exposed !

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.330
Damage has been inflicted
on the second tier !

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.710
Should we bring back our fleet ?

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.550
Don't panic.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.630
That would play right
into the enemy's plan.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:46.100
If they force a parallel pursuit like
the last time, then what would we do ?

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.000
But...

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.530
Counterattack with
the floating cannons !

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.700
It's looking good.
Just one more push !

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.260
E...enemy ships are...

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:14.310
An enemy ambush !

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.560
We've suffered direct
hits from port side !

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:16.800
Dammit !

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.730
Their missile ships
are defensively weak.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:25.090
We'll break through their fleet immediately
and then launch attacks on the main fleets.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.430
The enemy fleet that broke through
Holland's fleet is coming directly toward us !

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:36.320
From 10 o'clock direction !

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:37.550
The number is
approximately 2,200 !

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:41.900
It looks like they're using our
strategy to their advantage.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:42.750
Incoming attack !

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.200
Move toward 2 o'clock
and avoid their attack !

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.240
No.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.320
That would put us in
the Thor Hammer's range.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:58.160
What ?

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:09.710
The Alliance fell right
into Reinhard's trap.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:13.920
As Reinhard proclaimed to Kircheis, his small fleet of 2,200 ships...

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.820
...made a large impact on the whole course of the battle.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:19.970
In that case, we'll just break
through them from the front side.

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.400
All ships, attack the enemy
in the 10 o'clock direction !

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.550
The power differential between the main
Alliance fleets and Reinhard's fleet...

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.500
...was nearly 15 to 1.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.110
In most cases, there's no way such a
small fleet could put up a good fight.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.710
But in this instance, the Alliance was not able
to use its power differential to its advantage.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:38.770
Because they could only proceed by avoiding
the Thor Hammer's range on one side...

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:44.300
...and the dangerous corridor on the other side, their fleet was deployed in a long, thin line...

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:48.900
...and the small number of ships at the front
of that line had to face Reinhard's fleet alone.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.120
Nonetheless, fire was exchanged
in the fiercest manner.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.020
Lord Reinhard...

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.890
So far, everything is
going according to plan.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:05.340
But if other Imperial Fleet units come out to
this area in search of glory of their own...

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.920
...the battlefield will fall into chaos
and the Thor Hammer cannot be used.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:09.850
If that happens...

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.200
Reinhard's misgivings became reality.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:18.620
At 22:10, as Reinhard had been monopolizing the center stage up to this point...

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:21.900
...other units of the Imperial Fleet came rushing into this area.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.500
The enemy ships are
extended in a long line.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.410
Break them into pieces
and destroy them one by one.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.900
Strategically speaking, Fleet Admiral
Muckenberger's order was not unsound.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.750
And to leave the
fate of the battle...

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.110
...to the flow of the present combat
situation wasn't necessarily a bad idea.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.900
But that was the perspective
from the Imperial side...

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.290
...and the Alliance wasn't as
easily separated as was hoped.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.560
Plus, the moment the Imperial
Fleet came rushing in...

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.530
...was the moment when the
Thor Hammer became useless.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:53.550
Chief General Officer Greenhill
took the advice of Captain Yang...

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:57.850
...and put the reserve force into
the battle to force a melee.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:03.300
The characteristics of the 6th Battle
of Iserlohn can be summed as...

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:10.230
...the abrupt change of plans from the initial
strategies on both sides that led to chaos.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:18.300
If Muckenberger were ruthlessly analytical he
would have disregarded Reinhard's battle area...

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.750
...and stuck with the initial plan
to use the Thor Hammer...

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.040
...no matter how the battle
against the Alliance progressed.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.300
Consequently, Reinhard was displeased...

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.650
...about essentially becoming the
cause of this chaotic situation.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:30.820
The enemy is smart, too.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:34.280
They put their reserve forces into
action at the most opportune time.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:35.480
You're right.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:40.710
Are you thinking about the strategy
when we almost fell into their trap ?

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.760
It could be
the same opponent.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.250
Maybe I was a
little too overconfident.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.470
I was feeling like a hunter,
rather than a fighter.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:56.470
I should have known that the enemy also has
a brain that can put up effective strategies.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:10:00.300
But I don't think there are many
people who could pull this off.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.330
Yes, it might
be just one guy.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:09.300
But whether it's one or many, if rebel force
commanders can get the better of me...

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.450
...how can I take hold and
rule this whole universe ?

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:17.920
It's not that you failed; it's only
that you gained a new experience.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:21.010
The only thing you're
still lacking is experience...

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:25.380
...and since you just added one now,
it's not such a bad thing, after all.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.940
Do you really think so ?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.650
Yes, from my heart.

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:31.440
You're right.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.410
I should look
at it that way.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:37.080
It's not like me, to dwell
over what's already done.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:37.970
Right.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.560
It doesn't suit you.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.340
All right then.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:44.980
We'll withdraw to
the fortress for now.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:47.440
It's meaningless for us to
stay in the middle of this melee.

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:51.030
But there are those who
find meaning in such chaos.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:53.750
The Rosenritter are
a prime example of such.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:59.620
Using their assault landing ship to execute
a daring plunge into the enemy ships...

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:06.050
...they would seize the ships in close combat
and use the ships' communication system...

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:08.300
...to call out to
their former commander.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.560
Hey, come out, Luneberg !

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:22.050
We've specially reserved an
express train to hell, just for you !

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.790
Or did you already run
away like a coward ?

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.330
Come out, come out, Luneberg !

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:32.680
If you come out, we'll express-mail
you to the dungeon of the netherworld !

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:35.750
The hellish witches
are waiting for you !

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.850
You'll look so handsome,
colored in that bloody red !

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:41.720
We've done fairly
well, haven't we...

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:45.560
What are you thinking ?

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.340
This isn't your private war !

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.170
It is our private war.

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:52.670
If we don't think of it like
that, we can't do our job.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:57.590
We haven't fallen so far as to
kill someone as a public service.

00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:58.730
Wha...

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.180
Wha...

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:14.880
Thus, the Rosenritter left bloody invitations
to Luneberg everywhere they went...

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:20.030
...and that soon became known to the
commanding offices of the Imperial Fleet.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:26.450
On December 5th, Luneberg was called in by Fleet Admiral Muckenberger.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:37.150
I don't have time,
Rear Admiral Luneberg...

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:43.590
...to concern myself with the fortune of just one admiral, whether it's you or someone else.

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:46.380
So what do you
want me to do ?

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.140
That goes without saying.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:51.320
It's a challenge
made directly to you.

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:54.230
Shouldn't you take
it up yourself ?

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.470
I see.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:02.560
I'm a man who forsook
his country twice.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:05.110
Now, the country's abandoning me.

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:07.440
I guess I can't
say it's unreasonable.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:16.960
He doesn't know this yet, but his wife has just
become an infamous criminal, a brother-killer.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.010
It's better for him if he
just dies on the battlefield.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:25.430
Because if he lives on, his life from now on
will have nothing to do with glory or honor.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:32.260
In any case, Lord Fleet Admiral,
you have so much to worry about.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:40.460
Come out, come out, Luneberg !

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:43.800
If you come out, we'll express-mail
you to the dungeon of the netherworld !

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:47.110
The hellish witches
are waiting for you !

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.940
You'll look so handsome,
colored in that bloody red !

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.150
Enemy ship
closing in !

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:55.650
It's an Imperial
assault-landing ship !

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.200
It's making
a run toward us !

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.280
Here comes Luneberg.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:24.150
In accordance with your request,
I came for you, Schenkopp.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:28.640
You're too green to qualify for the position
of tour guide, but I'm a benevolent man.

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:35.010
Back off, Blumhart.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:39.460
I don't know about five years ago,
but you can't beat him at this point.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:47.170
Yeah, take a back seat, little chicky with
pieces of eggshell still hanging on your butt.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.610
You're finished, Luneberg !

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.840
Any last words ?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.400
Yeah, I'll say one thing.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:51.290
It's not that your skills improved,
Schenkopp, you greenhorn.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:54.050
It's only that my
skills deteriorated.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:56.170
Otherwise I would
never have lost.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:00.300
That may be the case.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:11.500
Elizabeth, I'll die for your sake, and I'll die
to liberate you, so do whatever you want.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:17.970
Salute him !

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:26.270
Whatever happened, he used to be our
leader, a courageous and heroic one.

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:38.720
After confirming Luneberg's death, the
Imperial assault-landing ship retreated.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:50.720
Schenkopp was experiencing a
fatigue-like weight on his shoulders.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:52.300
At a time like this...

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:57.070
...he wanted to see the woman who would have
given him silent sympathy and understanding.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:02.050
What he had lost on Vanfleet
4-2 was not insignificant.

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:08.390
While at the base to receive supplies and rest
his crew, Reinhard was called in by Kesler...

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:11.350
...who had been
looking for him.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.940
There had been a
new report from Odin.

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:16.440
Is it good news ?

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.080
I can't say so.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.350
Regrettably, it is an obituary.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.140
Did Admiral Grimmelshausen pass away ?

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:29.100
No, the one who passed away was the
Ministry of Interior Police Commissioner...

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:30.370
...Count Hartenberg.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.300
The Count was killed by his sister.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:40.550
And his sister, Elizabeth, is the
wife of Rear Admiral Luneberg.

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:48.210
To begin with, the source
of all the problems was...

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:52.980
...that Countess Elizabeth von Hartenberg
fell in love with Carl Mathius von Folgen.

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:59.050
Carl Mathius was, like many
aristocratic descendants...

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:02.670
...a profligate who couldn't learn to
live in a way that makes ends meet.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:06.960
On the other hand, Count
Hartenberg was a stoic individual...

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:12.550
...who was characterized as a natural-born
policeman who happened to be an aristocrat.

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:17.750
Naturally, he questioned Carl Mathius on how
he planned to support his life with Elizabeth.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:24.740
Cornered by this predicament, Carl Mathius decided to earn the necessary money through illegal means.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:26.580
"Illegal means" ?

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.140
Yes, he lent his hand to the
smuggling of the Thyoxin drug.

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:35.510
But Count Hartenberg
found out about it.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.230
He must have been devastated,
for his future brother-in-law...

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:43.350
...had just became a hardcore
criminal deserving capital punishment.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:45.350
It's not only that his sister
wouldn't live a happy life...

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:49.110
...but also that his future as a
police bureaucrat would also end.

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:53.680
So Count Hartenberg decided to
take care of the matter privately.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:58.460
First, he disclosed the whole story to
Carl Mathius' brother, Count Folgen...

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:01.450
...and made him an
accomplice to his scheme.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:06.700
Soon afterwards, Counts Hartenberg and
Folgen put pressure on the military office...

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:10.530
...and Carl Mathius was sent to
the front line as an officer...

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:12.150
...and died an "honorable"
death on the battlefield.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:17.270
In other words, Count Hartenberg sent
his sister's fiancé to the battlefield...

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:22.170
...in order to kill him and
protect his dishonorable secret.

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.840
Correct.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:26.700
Aristocratic society, the
police, and the military...

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:31.020
...all cooperated in order to
privately execute Carl Mathius.

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:37.070
Put in other words, because he was an
aristocrat he was allowed an honorable death.

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:40.520
After all, he was posthumously promoted
two ranks and became a Rear Admiral.

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:43.720
And his funeral was carried
out with full honors.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:45.750
So he became a hero.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:46.560
But...

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:50.920
The problem was the
bereaved Elizabeth.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:56.050
As she became a widow before marriage it seems she became a completely different person.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.250
I don't know the whole
truth on this point...

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:04.250
...but I speculate that the Count must have
loved his sister deeply in his own way...

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:06.890
...and seeing how his sister
became mentally disabled...

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:10.500
...he may have pushed her
marriage to Luneberg.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.980
But why did it
have to be Luneberg ?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.700
This is also
my conjecture...

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:22.920
...but the fact that he had been an enemy
till recently may have been the key.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:26.450
Carl Mathius was rumored to have
been killed by the Rosenritter.

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:32.740
It's a twisted psychology, but he may
have planned to invigorate her psyche...

00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:36.710
...by giving her a husband as
a target of her abhorrence.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.020
But what did Luneberg
think about that ?

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:43.050
Luneberg may have thought to
reinforce his position in the Empire...

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:46.170
...by becoming a part of
the Hartenberg family.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:48.500
But during the
course of things...

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:52.130
...he may have adopted the same
psychology as Count Hartenberg.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:54.700
To his wife who doesn't open up her heart
to him, he may have said something like...

00:20:54.700 --> 00:21:00.510
"I killed your former fiancé,
so hate me if you dare."

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:08.550
But whether love or hate, her feelings
were never directed toward Luneberg.

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:09.730
Meaning ?

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:12.700
On December 1st...

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:17.160
...Count Hartenberg received an invitation
from his sister to come to the Luneberg house.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:24.750
During that meeting the Count was fiercely accused of responsibility in Carl Mathius's death.

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:29.530
After a heated argument,
he stood up to leave the house.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:35.500
But as he was leaving, he was pushed
down the stairs from behind, by his sister.

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:40.700
It was later found that
his coffee was drugged...

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:45.520
...explaining why a strong man
like him was so easily pushed.

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:55.400
It's said that Count's face did
not retain its original features...

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:58.050
...that it became a mere
chunk of blood and meat.

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:01.830
There's one thing that
I don't understand.

00:22:01.830 --> 00:22:08.370
How did Mrs. Luneberg find out that her brother was responsible for her fiancé's death ?

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:12.560
That has something to do
with Lord Grimmelshausen.

00:22:13.550 --> 00:22:14.540
Please take a look at this.

00:22:15.670 --> 00:22:20.220
His Lordship has kept all the secrets he
has learned in the 76 years of his life...

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:22.700
...the unknown occurrences
in military, aristocratic...

00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:27.110
...bureaucratic societies,
and studiously recorded them.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:29.420
This book is where
he recorded them.

00:22:29.420 --> 00:22:33.460
Lord Grimmelshausen was aware
that his life might end soon...

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:36.840
...so he gave a few pages of
this book to Mrs. Luneberg...

00:22:36.840 --> 00:22:39.720
...so that she might decide her course
of action through her own will.

00:22:41.600 --> 00:22:44.460
What do you plan to do with
that book, Captain Kesler ?

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:47.660
The book was not
left to my discretion.

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:49.860
It's been left up
to you, Admiral Musel.

00:22:50.460 --> 00:22:51.780
Me ?

00:22:52.630 --> 00:22:57.170
Lord Grimmelshausen has decided
to entrust this book to you.

00:22:57.900 --> 00:23:02.200
He asks that you take charge
of this book upon his death.

00:23:02.200 --> 00:23:05.050
And I've accepted
being the messenger.

00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:09.860
He said that he'd like the book
to be of use to you, Admiral Musel.

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:12.430
Of use to me ?

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:19.320
This book records many wrongdoings and secrets of lineage aristocrats and bureaucrats.

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:22.700
I hope that you'll
use this book...

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:26.150
...to reinforce your standing and
help yourself in future battles.

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:31.270
I very much appreciate
Lord Grimmelshausen's favor.

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:34.370
But I will not
be a blackmailer.

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:37.950
I am grateful that his Lordship
has committed this to me, but...

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:41.830
Kircheis here knows this.

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:45.720
I am a military officer, and I would like to
make my future only through my own talents...

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:48.250
...and capabilities
as a military officer.

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:53.700
If I'm to be detested by lineage aristocrats
and bureaucrats in the end anyway...

00:23:53.700 --> 00:23:56.700
...I'd like to be detested
in a dignified way.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:00.750
To be abhorred and loathed for being
a blackmailer is not what I want to do.

00:24:02.060 --> 00:24:05.270
Then are you going to
throw this book away ?

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:13.700
No, I will trust you, as
Lord Grimmelshausen trusts you.

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:18.870
So I will ask you: can you put this document
under seal and take custody of it ?

00:24:18.870 --> 00:24:20.390
Until when ?

00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:25.170
Until such a time when history is no
longer monopolized by the aristocracy.

00:24:33.110 --> 00:24:34.290
I understand.

00:24:34.290 --> 00:24:35.900
I'll do as you instruct.

00:24:37.110 --> 00:24:42.170
I will seal this document and will keep it out of others' hands as much as possible within my power.

00:24:47.920 --> 00:24:49.670
Then I will go now.

00:24:50.540 --> 00:24:54.170
As soon as the battle ends,
I will have to depart.

00:24:54.170 --> 00:24:56.410
I may not be able
to see you again.

00:24:57.150 --> 00:24:58.990
Are you going back to Odin ?

00:24:58.990 --> 00:25:04.070
I will return to Odin and then transfer to
one of the governments on the frontier.

00:25:04.070 --> 00:25:05.530
Frontier government ?

00:25:05.530 --> 00:25:09.600
I'm not very well-liked among the
high-ranking military officials.

00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:12.250
Through my acquaintance
with Lord Grimmelshausen...

00:25:12.250 --> 00:25:14.700
...I have been allowed
to remain on Odin.

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:17.500
But that will only last while
his Lordship is still alive.

00:25:20.250 --> 00:25:24.560
The duration of postings at frontier governments is three years according to the regulation...

00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:27.250
...but there are many that are sent from one
frontier to another throughout their lifetime...

00:25:27.250 --> 00:25:31.050
...as they're disliked
by the military officials.

00:25:31.050 --> 00:25:34.410
I will probably be
one of those cases.

00:25:34.410 --> 00:25:36.170
And are you
okay with that ?

00:25:36.720 --> 00:25:42.940
It's not an ideal situation, but I don't have the
power to reverse military officials' orders.

00:25:42.940 --> 00:25:47.100
So I'd like to govern myself and hold to my own standards, so as not to be servile.

00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:53.360
Kesler !

00:25:55.650 --> 00:26:00.800
Three years from now, I will be in a position of much more power than I am now.

00:26:00.800 --> 00:26:07.080
At that time, I will recall you to Odin and assign you to a position that best suits your ability.

00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:09.760
So can you wait till then ?

00:26:27.600 --> 00:26:34.070
The 6th Battle of Iserlohn was, though near the end, still becoming increasingly fierce.

00:26:30.320 --> 00:26:36.100
The 6th Battle of Iserlohn

00:26:37.340 --> 00:26:42.050
Preview of Next Episode

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:40.110
Though the Alliance succeeded in turning the battle into a melee...

00:26:40.110 --> 00:26:44.600
...they couldn't get a strong enough hold to attack the fortress and the battle stayed static.

00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:47.530
To put an end to the stalemate,
Yang recommends withdrawal.

00:26:47.530 --> 00:26:51.300
But before then, Reinhard lures
the Alliance into his trap...

00:26:51.300 --> 00:26:56.210
...and the Thor Hammer finally unleashes
its overwhelmingly destructive fire.

00:26:56.690 --> 00:26:58.050
Next episode of...

00:26:57.200 --> 00:27:07.340
Legend of the Galactic Heroes Gaiden

00:26:57.200 --> 00:27:07.340
One Hundred Billion Stars,
One Hundred Billion Lights
Final Chapter
"One Hundred Billion Stars, One Ambition"

00:27:04.100 --> 00:27:06.370
Men's ambitions fly through the galaxy.
